1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,423
Chai Corner now has two
outlets, and ten people.

2
00:00:03,723 --> 00:00:05,597
But nobody is sure who does what.

3
00:00:06,147 --> 00:00:09,436
Two people make the tea,
and nobody washes the cups.

4
00:00:09,736 --> 00:00:12,877
Office orders get lost,
because nobody owns them.

5
00:00:13,177 --> 00:00:15,844
And every small question
still goes to Ravi.

6
00:00:16,494 --> 00:00:18,324
Ravi doesn't need more hands.

7
00:00:18,324 --> 00:00:19,769
He needs a structure.

8
00:00:20,469 --> 00:00:22,192
So, what is organizing?

9
00:00:22,492 --> 00:00:27,008
Organizing means arranging people
and resources, so the work gets done.

10
00:00:27,358 --> 00:00:29,179
Everyone gets a clear role.

11
00:00:29,179 --> 00:00:30,857
That is, what they do.

12
00:00:31,207 --> 00:00:32,355
Clear authority.

13
00:00:32,355 --> 00:00:34,474
That is, the power to decide.

14
00:00:34,824 --> 00:00:36,407
And clear relationships.

15
00:00:36,407 --> 00:00:38,504
That is, who reports to whom.

16
00:00:39,154 --> 00:00:41,471
Ravi organizes in five steps.

17
00:00:41,921 --> 00:00:42,821
One.

18
00:00:42,446 --> 00:00:44,128
Identify the activities.

19
00:00:44,128 --> 00:00:47,717
Boil tea, serve, take
cash, wash cups, deliver.

20
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:48,967
Two.

21
00:00:48,630 --> 00:00:49,648
Group them.

22
00:00:49,648 --> 00:00:51,571
Similar jobs go together.

23
00:00:51,921 --> 00:00:52,821
Three.

24
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:53,679
Assign duties.

25
00:00:53,679 --> 00:00:57,120
Asha leads the kitchen,
and Kabir runs the cash.

26
00:00:57,471 --> 00:00:58,371
Four.

27
00:00:58,066 --> 00:00:59,469
Delegate authority.

28
00:00:59,469 --> 00:01:01,977
That means handing some power down.

29
00:01:01,977 --> 00:01:04,326
Asha can now order milk herself.

30
00:01:04,676 --> 00:01:05,576
And five.

31
00:01:05,524 --> 00:01:06,424
Coordinate.

32
00:01:06,414 --> 00:01:09,558
Link every group, so
they work as one team.

33
00:01:10,208 --> 00:01:12,768
That second step has a special name.

34
00:01:12,768 --> 00:01:13,918
Departmentation.

35
00:01:14,268 --> 00:01:17,140
It means grouping
activities into departments.

36
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:19,934
Right now, everyone is in one big group.

37
00:01:20,284 --> 00:01:22,882
There are five common ways to split it.

38
00:01:22,882 --> 00:01:24,171
Watch Ravi's chart.

39
00:01:24,621 --> 00:01:25,521
Functional.

40
00:01:25,513 --> 00:01:26,634
Group by job.

41
00:01:26,634 --> 00:01:29,488
Kitchen, cash, cleaning, and delivery.

42
00:01:29,888 --> 00:01:32,478
Territorial, also called geographical.

43
00:01:32,478 --> 00:01:33,705
Group by place.

44
00:01:33,705 --> 00:01:35,785
Outlet one, and outlet two.

45
00:01:36,185 --> 00:01:37,085
Product.

46
00:01:36,883 --> 00:01:38,555
Group by what you sell.

47
00:01:38,555 --> 00:01:39,913
Chai, and snacks.

48
00:01:40,313 --> 00:01:41,213
Customer.

49
00:01:41,095 --> 00:01:42,847
Group by who you serve.

50
00:01:42,847 --> 00:01:45,370
Walk-in customers, and office orders.

51
00:01:45,770 --> 00:01:46,670
And process.

52
00:01:46,623 --> 00:01:48,576
Group by the steps of the work.

53
00:01:48,576 --> 00:01:50,502
Boiling, brewing, and serving.

54
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:53,029
No single way is best.

55
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:54,372
Ravi mixes two.

56
00:01:54,722 --> 00:01:57,740
Outlets first, then
jobs inside each outlet.

57
00:01:58,090 --> 00:02:01,053
Now everyone knows their
job, and their boss.

58
00:02:01,053 --> 00:02:04,266
And small questions stop
at Meena, at outlet two.

59
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:05,883
Quick check.

60
00:02:05,883 --> 00:02:10,190
Ravi makes one team for office
orders, and one for walk-in buyers.

61
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:11,625
Which type is this?

62
00:02:13,525 --> 00:02:14,425
Customer!

63
00:02:14,214 --> 00:02:16,690
The teams are grouped by who they serve.

64
00:02:17,290 --> 00:02:18,299
So, remember.

65
00:02:18,599 --> 00:02:22,456
Organizing gives everyone a
clear role, authority, and boss.

66
00:02:22,806 --> 00:02:27,675
It takes five steps: identify, group,
assign, delegate, and coordinate.

67
00:02:28,025 --> 00:02:32,226
And departments can be built by
function, territory, product, customer,

68
00:02:32,226 --> 00:02:33,126
or process.

69
00:02:33,667 --> 00:02:35,209
Next time, staffing.

70
00:02:35,209 --> 00:02:38,776
How Ravi finds, hires, and
trains the right people.
